Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a blend's line (BRepBlend_Line) held its points in an
NCollection_Sequence, whose access by index walks its linked list from the
place read last. The approximation of a blend's surface
(BRepBlend_AppFuncRoot::SearchPoint) finds the points around each parameter
it evaluates by a bisection over the line, reads the line's middle point
for a ball that stays put (mitcad#1412) and inserts the points that took
long to solve: every evaluation walked the line several times over, and on
a long line the approximation spent nearly all its time in those walks
(mitcad#1823: a ring's window sills rounded away, 562 s, 90 % of the stack
samples in NCollection_BaseSequence::Find). The points are now held in a
deque of their own allocations, read by index in constant time; each
point keeps its address while others are added or removed, as a
sequence's node did, and the line's order, contents and range checks are
those of the sequence, so every algorithm reads the same points.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1690.

